    {
      "id": "claim_99956f86a5cd4599b96d8ea0296e6b17",
      "statement": "Fleet proofs use follower nodes: up to two recruited followers (never the owner itself), each must fsync; one follower keeps the fleet acknowledging; a takeover seals the prior node-log session before restoring, and each process session creates a conditional node-log record before its first fleet-durable acknowledgement that a cold activation must resolve (absent/sealed/open→recovery) before restoring.",
      "evidence": [
