    {
      "id": "claim_b5136ca428a44592bfa0ae3851086fb6",
      "statement": "WAL truncation and deadlines: CELLD_LTX_TRUNCATE_PAGES (default 128 pages, 512 KiB) truncates an ordinary cell's WAL at the next checkpoint because a passive checkpoint does not shrink the file; queue cells use passive checkpoints because truncation emits a full database image; CELLD_LTX_DURABILITY_TIMEOUT_SECS (default 10) bounds durability proofs and the final snapshot retry window; fault tests confirm a SIGKILL'd write stream loses no acknowledged write and a throttled bucket (429) slows the engine to the store write rate without amplifying.",
